"use strict";(self.webpackChunksite=self.webpackChunksite||[]).push([[4221],{2610:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"newsletter-vol-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/newsletter-vol-2","editUrl":"https://github.com/tue-datastewards/research-data-management-handbook/tree/main/blog/2026-07-01-newsletter-vol-2-rdm-policy/index.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-07-01-newsletter-vol-2-rdm-policy/index.md","title":"Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 2: RDM Policy, DataBites, FAIR Clinic & more","description":"Cover of the TU/e Research Data Management Framework Policy","date":"2026-07-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"newsletter","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/tags/newsletter","description":"Research Data Stewards newsletters"},{"inline":false,"label":"data stewards","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/tags/data-stewards","description":"Topics related to data stewards"}],"readingTime":2.89,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"TU/e Data Stewards","title":"Research Data Management team","url":"https://rdm.tue.nl/docs/contact","page":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/authors/data-stewards"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/tue-datastewards.png","key":"data-stewards"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"newsletter-vol-2","title":"Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 2: RDM Policy, DataBites, FAIR Clinic & more","authors":["data-stewards"],"tags":["newsletter","data-stewards"],"image":"./rdm-policy.jpg"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Highlight of Data Steward Team for 2025","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/highlight-2025"}},"content":"![Cover of the TU/e Research Data Management Framework Policy](rdm-policy.jpg)\\n\\nIn this newsletter, we highlight the new TU/e Research Data Management Policy, the Research Cockpit, DataBites, the FAIR Data Clinic and the Open Science Community Eindhoven.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n_This post is an archived version of the Research Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 2, originally sent in July 2026._\\n\\n## RDM Policy\\n\\nDid you know that TU/e has a brand new Research Data Management Policy?\\n\\nThe TU/e Research Data Management Framework Policy defines roles and responsibilities for researchers and research support staff regarding the management of research data.\\n\\nYou can learn more about the policy and what it means to you on the [RDM Handbook page](/docs/intro/tue-policy/).\\n\\n[Learn more about the RDM Policy](/docs/intro/tue-policy/)\\n\\n## What\'s new in the Research Cockpit?\\n\\nAs part of being compliant with the RDM Policy, we have developed the Research Cockpit, a one-stop shop for researchers where you can find templates for your data management plan, ethical application, data sharing agreements and much more.\\n\\nIn this newsletter, we would like to highlight one of its services:\\n\\n### RAPS: Research Archival Packaging Solution\\n\\nRAPS is a closed TU/e archive for the data underlying your article once it is accepted for publication in a scientific peer-reviewed journal. RAPS preserves this research data for the long term.\\n\\n[Go to RAPS](https://cockpit.research.tue.nl/servicedesk/customer/portal/7)\\n\\n## DataBites\\n\\nDataBites is a series of online sessions designed to spread awareness on various topics related to research data management. Each session features a quick 15-minute talk or demo, followed by a 15-minute chat, focusing on one specific RDM topic. From RDM essentials, FAIR principles, documentation, versioning and storage to preparing data for publishing (to name just a few).\\n\\n[Join DataBites](/docs/learning-resources/data-bites/)\\n\\n## FAIR Data Clinic\\n\\nDo you care about your data having an impact beyond your papers?\\n\\nJoin our monthly FAIR Data Clinic: a practical session in which we help you make your dataset ready for repository deposit.\\n\\n[Sign up for the FAIR Data Clinic](/docs/learning-resources/fair-clinic/)\\n\\n## Open Science Community Eindhoven\\n\\nThe community is a growing group of researchers, engineers, scientists and university faculty who care about transparency and quality in science.\\n\\nOur goal is to form an inclusive community of people working on improving the way we conduct open science at Eindhoven University of Technology, and to help others do the same.\\n\\n[Learn more about OSC Eindhoven](https://osceindhoven.nl/)\\n\\n## Trivia from data stewards: The Mere-Exposure Effect\\n\\n![Andy Warhol\'s Campbell\'s Soup Cans](https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Campbell%27s_Soup_Cans_by_Andy_Warhol.jpg/960px-Campbell%27s_Soup_Cans_by_Andy_Warhol.jpg)\\n\\n_Andy Warhol\'s Campbell\'s Soup Cans paintings displayed at the Museum of Modern Art. Photographed by Brandon Fick, 12 May 2006. Source: Flickr. Licensed under CC BY 2.0._\\n\\nDid you know that simply seeing something repeatedly makes you like it more, even if you do not realize it? Psychologists call this phenomenon the \\"mere-exposure effect\\". This is one reason why advertisers repeat their messages.\\n\\nThe effect highlights the power of the environment on us. Feeling a bit helpless? We can curate what we surround ourselves with to influence our preferences. Do you have something that you do not enjoy but want to do for the greater good? Perhaps you find making data FAIR challenging, but you want to do so for open science? You can surround yourself with things that you would like to overcome and let familiarity do its work. Keep the [RDM Handbook](https://rdm.tue.nl/) on your desk, join a [DataBites session](/docs/learning-resources/data-bites/), or sign up for a [FAIR Data Clinic](/docs/learning-resources/fair-clinic/). Let\'s design our environment to conquer our own resistance.\\n\\n_Nami (social psychology)_\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Subscribe to the Research Data Stewards newsletter](https://par.copernica.tue.nl/)"},{"id":"highlight-2025","metadata":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/highlight-2025","editUrl":"https://github.com/tue-datastewards/research-data-management-handbook/tree/main/blog/2025-11-19-highlight-2025/index.md","source":"@site/blog/2025-11-19-highlight-2025/index.md","title":"Highlight of Data Steward Team for 2025","description":"We are approaching the end of 2025! As the Data Steward team, we discussed what is one highlight for our team.","date":"2025-11-19T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"data stewards","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/tags/data-stewards","description":"Topics related to data stewards"}],"readingTime":1.58,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Nami Sunami","title":"Data Steward","url":"https://namisunami.com","page":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/authors/nsunami"},"socials":{"bluesky":"https://bsky.app/profile/namisunami.com","github":"https://github.com/nsunami","mastodon":"https://mastodon.social/@nsunami@akademienl.social","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nsunami/"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/nsunami.png","key":"nsunami"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"highlight-2025","title":"Highlight of Data Steward Team for 2025","authors":["nsunami"],"tags":["data-stewards"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 2: RDM Policy, DataBites, FAIR Clinic & more","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/newsletter-vol-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Welcome to the RDM Handbook!","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/welcome-to-rdm-handbook"}},"content":"We are approaching the end of 2025! As the Data Steward team, we discussed what is one highlight for our team.\\n\\n## What was our highlight for 2025?\\n\\nWe had many options, such as installing the [TU/e Research Data Management Framework Policy](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15309046), engaging with the researcher community, enhancing the Research Cockpit... In the end, we decided that making the [Research Data Management Booklet](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15736839) was our highlight for the year!\\n\\n![Three Research Data Management Booklets standing, with the cover page showing the text, \\"This is RDM\\"](rdm-booklets.png)\\n\\nYou can download the booklet on Zenodo: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15736840\\n\\nIf you want physical copies, please [contact us](/docs/contact).\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Information we submitted as product team highlight 2025\\n\\nBelow is the information about the RDM Booklet project.\\n\\n### Approach\\n\\nThree years ago there was an initiative to make an RDM Booklet for newly onboarded researchers, only last year a data steward picked this up again and made all the necessary updates. The Booklet got feedback from all the relevant stakeholders and was sent to the printers in September this year.\\n\\n### Results\\n\\nThe data steward team developed a booklet to help new students and researchers managing their research data\\n\\n### Timeline\\n\\nThe initial plan started on 2022, but due to capacity issues it got postponed. In 2025 this project was picked up again and brought to fulfillment this September 2025\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nEarly-career researchers are now more aware of RDM and who to ask for support if they need more in-dept help.\\n\\n### Feedback Received\\n\\nThis booklet has received very positive feedback form early-career researchers that need guidance in RDM. We have been providing these booklets at onboarding events, Research Day, LIS Expo, Responsible Research conversations event, etc.\\n\\n### Lessons Learned\\n\\n- Clear communication\\n- Re-usability of materials\\n- Visual design skills\\n- Evaluation of the needs from researchers\\n- Engaging with all the relevant stakeholders\\n- Feedback gathering and implementation"},{"id":"welcome-to-rdm-handbook","metadata":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/welcome-to-rdm-handbook","editUrl":"https://github.com/tue-datastewards/research-data-management-handbook/tree/main/blog/2025-05-01-welcome-to-rdm-handbook/index.md","source":"@site/blog/2025-05-01-welcome-to-rdm-handbook/index.md","title":"Welcome to the RDM Handbook!","description":"Welcome to the Handbook!","date":"2025-05-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"data stewards","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/tags/data-stewards","description":"Topics related to data stewards"}],"readingTime":0.53,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Nami Sunami","title":"Data Steward","url":"https://namisunami.com","page":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/authors/nsunami"},"socials":{"bluesky":"https://bsky.app/profile/namisunami.com","github":"https://github.com/nsunami","mastodon":"https://mastodon.social/@nsunami@akademienl.social","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/nsunami/"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/nsunami.png","key":"nsunami"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome-to-rdm-handbook","title":"Welcome to the RDM Handbook!","authors":["nsunami"],"tags":["data-stewards"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Highlight of Data Steward Team for 2025","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/highlight-2025"},"nextItem":{"title":"Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 1: Launch of the Research Cockpit","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/newsletter-vol-1"}},"content":"Welcome to the Handbook!\\n\\n## Our Mission\\n\\nOur mission as Data Stewards is to help researchers with Research Data Management (RDM) challenges in a collaborative way, while being an advocate of open & responsible scientific practices that transcend TU/e.\\n\\n## What we offer\\n\\n- First-line support for researchers on Research Data Management (RDM), privacy, ethics, and data agreements for researchers\\n- Consultations for workflows related to Data Management & FAIR data\\n- Training and knowledge transfer on RDM, privacy, and associated topics\\n\\n## Get in touch\\n\\nTo contact data stewards, please email [rdmsupport@tue.nl](mailto:rdmsupport@tue.nl). Or contact your faculty data steward directly, as listed below.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e"},{"id":"newsletter-vol-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/newsletter-vol-1","editUrl":"https://github.com/tue-datastewards/research-data-management-handbook/tree/main/blog/2024-11-20-newsletter-vol-1-research-cockpit/index.md","source":"@site/blog/2024-11-20-newsletter-vol-1-research-cockpit/index.md","title":"Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 1: Launch of the Research Cockpit","description":"Screenshot of the Research Cockpit","date":"2024-11-20T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"newsletter","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/tags/newsletter","description":"Research Data Stewards newsletters"},{"inline":false,"label":"data stewards","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/tags/data-stewards","description":"Topics related to data stewards"}],"readingTime":1.74,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"TU/e Data Stewards","title":"Research Data Management team","url":"https://rdm.tue.nl/docs/contact","page":{"permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/authors/data-stewards"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/tue-datastewards.png","key":"data-stewards"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"newsletter-vol-1","title":"Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 1: Launch of the Research Cockpit","authors":["data-stewards"],"tags":["newsletter","data-stewards"],"image":"./research-cockpit.jpg"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Welcome to the RDM Handbook!","permalink":"/pr-preview/pr-286/blog/welcome-to-rdm-handbook"}},"content":"![Screenshot of the Research Cockpit](research-cockpit.jpg)\\n\\nWe are pleased to announce the launch of the Research Cockpit, a new system designed to assist researchers in managing their research data. This platform will evolve gradually, with additional products and services being introduced over time to support the entire research data lifecycle.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n_This post is an archived version of the Research Data Stewards Newsletter Vol. 1, originally sent in November 2024._\\n\\n## Launch of the Research Cockpit\\n\\nThe Research Cockpit brings together the tools, templates and support that researchers need throughout the research data lifecycle. It is the central place to find help with data management plans, ethical applications, data sharing agreements and more.\\n\\n[Go to the Research Cockpit](https://cockpit.research.tue.nl/)\\n\\n## Meet your data stewards\\n\\nThe data stewards support researchers in all faculties. At the time of this newsletter, the team consisted of:\\n\\n| Data steward           | Faculty / role                                    |\\n| ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Liz Guzman-Ramirez     | Team lead                                         |\\n| Angela Aleksovska      | Electrical Engineering                            |\\n| Davide Nardi           | Mathematics and Computer Science                  |\\n| Jay Nair               | Industrial Engineering & Innovation Sciences      |\\n| Lucia Forrov\xe1          | Built Environment                                 |\\n| Neda Nozouri           | Biomedical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering    |\\n| Mariana Oshima Menegon | Industrial Design                                 |\\n| Nami Sunami            | Chemical Engineering & Chemistry, Applied Physics |\\n\\nSee the [contact page](/docs/contact) for the current team.\\n\\n## What can we help you with?\\n\\n- Funder requirements related to RDM\\n- Research data storage solutions\\n- Publishing data and software\\n- Ethics applications and informed consent forms\\n- Implementation of FAIR data\\n- Privacy questions\\n- Data management plans\\n- Legal agreements and impact assessments\\n\\n[Read more about the data stewards](<https://tuenl.sharepoint.com/sites/intranet-LIS/SitePages/Data-stewards(1).aspx>)\\n\\n## Trivia from data stewards: Planetary Nebula\\n\\n![Planetary nebula](planetary-nebula.jpg)\\n\\nDid you know that when our Sun starts to die, for a brief period of time (in astronomical time scales), it will become a planetary nebula? We think it will look something like this, with the outer layers reaching the orbit of the Earth.\\n\\n_Liz (astrophysics)_\\n\\n---\\n\\n[Subscribe to the Research Data Stewards newsletter](https://par.copernica.tue.nl/)"}]}}')}}]);